          ":question/problem": "For $f(x,y)=\\left(x + y^{2}\\right) \\left(- y + \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}\\right)$, evaluate $f_y(4,3)$. Assume $(x,y)\\ne(0,0)$.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Differentiate with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as constant. Write $f=Cuv+r$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nC&=1,\\quad r=0\\\\\nu&=x + y^{2},\\quad v=- y + \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the power, sum, and chain rules on the active factors gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu_y&=2 y\\\\\nv_y&=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}} - 1\\\\\nr_y&=0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply both terms of the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y&=C(u_yv+uv_y)+r_y\\\\\n&=2 y \\left(- y + \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad +\\left(\\left(x + y^{2}\\right) \\left(\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}} - 1\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow substitute $x=4$ and $y=3$ and combine the exact values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y(4,3)&=\\left(6\\right)\\left(2\\right)+\\left(13\\right)\\left(- \\frac{2}{5}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{34}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
